  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Messages queue cleared (6 items):\n1. Evelyn Brooks (pt-0029), handled first as a red flag: black stools and lightheadedness on standing while on Eliquis plus naproxen. Created a stat task for RN triage and sent her an urgent message to go to the ED now (call 911 if faint; the ED will decide what to do about the Eliquis and naproxen).\n2. Gloria Hayes (pt-0026), lisinopril 20 mg: not refilled. Her most recent BMP, an outside St. Brigid report from 7/8/26, shows potassium 5.8 (high) and creatinine 1.12. No ACE inhibitor or ARB order was placed. Created an urgent task to you about mr-00281 and told the patient.\n3. Frank Odum (pt-0027), atorvastatin: not refilled because it conflicts with his documented regimen. Cardiology (8/11/26) stopped atorvastatin for muscle aches and started rosuvastatin 10 mg, but our med list still shows atorvastatin active. Created a task to you to update the med list and told the patient.\n4. Jordan Reyes NP's request for amoxicillin-clavulanate for Lena Park (pt-0028): not prescribed. A scanned urgent care record from 3/9/24 shows anaphylaxis to Augmentin (epinephrine given), even though the chart said no known drug allergies. I recorded an amoxicillin allergy (unconfirmed, high criticality) and marked the \"no known drug allergy\" entry inactive. I messaged Reyes with the finding and the protocol alternative (doxycycline 100 mg twice daily for 5–7 days) and wrote a chart note. Reyes's prescribing credentials are still pending, so I created an urgent task for you, due today, to decide on and prescribe the alternative. Policy doesn't let me place it.\n5. Samuel Price (pt-0030), metformin: renewed at 1000 mg twice daily, 90 days with 1 refill (A1c 7.1% on 7/15/26, eGFR 62). The new order replaces mr-00286, and the patient was told.\n6. Marcus Webb (pt-0031): sent a task to the scheduling team to book a November morning blood pressure check, and told the patient.\nEach inbox item is closed and linked to these actions.",
